	)
	(text "CS_CTRL, CS_HV, DAC_LDAC_N and DAC_RESET_N must remain high\nthroughout an intended WRITE pulse. A change suppresses the\napplied window and raises MAT_CONFIG_TRIP. VMM DAC chip\nselects are not included. READ may intentionally sweep its\nsource DAC while the route remains fixed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 510.54 219.965 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.08 1.08)
				(color 0 70 160 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cb7d9947-4747-4210-867d-3e4e0db92f42")
	)
	(text "Stored energy and pulse timing"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 510.54 351.79 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.35 1.35)
				(color 0 70 160 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ccadf722-3b69-4a95-983f-16eda00c2ba6")
	)
	(text "Use at least 1 us between the qualified LATCH edge and OE_N\nfalling for the digital paths here; analog settling is\nadditional and range dependent. A fault requires source\nzero, explicit clear release and a new full frame plus\nqualified commit. Never change OE while LATCH is high."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 510.54 311.405 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.08 1.08)
				(color 0 70 160 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ce4f7343-5f49-4f16-b3cc-17cb697cee23")
	)
	(text "Two 74LVC574 registers capture SRC, RSH, POLARITY, BL and\nNL addresses plus exclusive service/read mode and request\nvalidity. Analog route controls use captured outputs. Two\n74HC688 comparators detect request changes; mismatch blocks\nRUN and generates a latched fault request while output is\nintended."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 510.54 128.525 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.08 1.08)
				(color 0 70 160 1)
			)
